takes your money."},{"t":1,"loc":"TAR","text":"At Hispania Tarraconensis, the old governor Servius Sulpicius Galba lets his men hail him: legate of the Senate and People, he says, not yet emperor."},{"t":2,"loc":"SYR","text":"XII Fulminata takes your promises."},{"t":2,"loc":"AFR","text":"In Africa, Clodius Macer, legate of III Augusta, holds back the grain ships and raises a legion of his own."},{"t":2,"loc":"GSU","text":"Titus Licinius Agricola, legate of XXII Primigenia, claims the purple in Germania Superior."},{"t":2,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Lucius Clodius Macer and Titus Licinius Agricola."},{"t":2,"loc":null,"text":"Lucius Clodius Macer has lost his last legion. His cause is finished."},{"t":3,"loc":"SYR","text":"Syria is yours."},{"t":3,"loc":"ROM","text":"Nero is dead. Abandoned by the Praetorians, he took his own life outside Rome. The Senate rules, for now."},{"t":3,"loc":null,"text":"Quintus Herennius Celer swears to you when your province falls: a legate of one of your legions. He can command an army or govern a province for you."},{"t":3,"loc":"MCA","text":"The Mauretanian chiefs send 3000 men to Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":4,"loc":null,"text":"Your legions hail you as imperator."},{"t":4,"loc":"ROM","text":"Nero's exiles come home and get their estates back. Their families remember who did it."},{"t":5,"loc":"ROM","text":"The Senate names you legate of the Senate and People of Rome."},{"t":5,"loc":"NIT","text":"Decimus Tettius Flaccus, legate of I Italica, claims the purple in Northern Italy."},{"t":5,"loc":"JUD","text":"Gaius Antonius Niger, legate of V Macedonica, claims the purple in Judaea."},{"t":5,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Decimus Tettius Flaccus and Titus Licinius Agricola."},{"t":5,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Gaius Antonius Niger and Servius Sulpicius Galba."}],"rel":{"galba|player":-30,"F7|macer":15,"F7|galba":-3,"F15|F7":15,"F16|galba":15},"treaties":[{"id":2,"type":"truce","a":"F15